# Build context for tools/local-test/Containerfile.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS, measured rather than assumed: without it the build
# transferred an 11 GB context. Build contexts do NOT read .gitignore, so every
# `.terraform/` provider directory in the working tree was sent to the daemon
# (23 of them, 18 GB on the host where this was measured) and landed in the two
# COPY layers of the provider-mirror step. The image is meant to be a small,
# reproducible offline check path; an 11 GB context defeats that.
#
# WHY THE DOCKER NAME for a file next to a Containerfile: Docker reads only
# `.dockerignore`, while Podman reads `.containerignore` AND falls back to
# `.dockerignore`. One file under this name therefore covers both engines that
# run.sh supports; a `.containerignore` would be silently ignored by Docker,
# which is the engine most likely to be used here. (BuildKit first looks for
# `tools/local-test/Containerfile.dockerignore` and falls back to this file at
# the context root.)
#
# It is an ALLOWLIST, not a list of exclusions, and that is deliberate. The
# Containerfile copies exactly five things (Containerfile:79, 93, 94, 114, 127):
#
#   COPY tools/local-test/requirements.txt -> pip install at build time
#   COPY modules                        -> provider mirror (needs the lock files)
#   COPY customizations                 -> provider mirror
#   COPY .tflint.hcl                    -> tflint --init at build time
#   COPY tools/local-test/entrypoint.sh -> the run-stage entrypoint
#
# With an allowlist, a COPY added later for a path not listed here FAILS the
# build with a missing source instead of silently shipping whatever else is in
# the tree — including the gitignored operator files under env/, which carry
# real account identifiers and must never enter an image layer. `env/` reaches
# the container at RUN time through the mount in run.sh, which is where it
# belongs. Failing loudly is the same choice the mirror step makes when a
# single module cannot mirror.
#
# That property proved itself immediately: the first build with this file
# stopped on `requirements.txt`, which the author of this list (the
# orchestrator) had missed when reading the COPY lines. A denylist would have
# built an image quietly missing nothing — and shipped 11 GB of context.

# Exclude everything, then re-admit only what the build copies.
*

!modules
!customizations
!.tflint.hcl
!tools/local-test/entrypoint.sh
!tools/local-test/requirements.txt

# ...but never the provider directories inside the re-admitted trees. This is
# the 18 GB, and it sits UNDER modules/, so the re-inclusion above would
# otherwise pull it straight back in. The tracked .terraform.lock.hcl files are
# deliberately NOT excluded: `terraform providers mirror` reads them to pick the
# exact version each module pins.
modules/**/.terraform
customizations/**/.terraform

# Test staging directories the live-test runner creates inside module trees.
modules/**/.livetest
customizations/**/.livetest
